# Cokonu — required environment variables (names only; NO secret values here).
# Copy to .env.local for local dev, and set the same keys in Netlify:
#   Project configuration → Environment variables.

# Live product catalog: Google Apps Script web app URL (the .../exec endpoint)
# that returns the catalog JSON. Read server-side only, in lib/catalog.ts via
# process.env.SHEETS_CATALOG_URL. Never commit the real value.
SHEETS_CATALOG_URL=

# Cloudinary — ORIGIN store for product photos (READ-ONLY: the site only lists
# what's there and serves the original delivery URLs; next/image still does the
# optimizing). Server-side only, read in lib/cloudinaryCatalog.ts.
# If these are unset the site simply serves the repo photos in public/products/,
# so local builds work without them. Set the real values in Netlify:
# Project configuration → Environment variables. Never commit them.
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
